# What EAS uploads for the openhome iOS build.
#
# EAS archives the whole GIT REPOSITORY, not the npm workspace, and MonoClaw's
# root holds ~50 unrelated projects (travelog 332 MB, projects 198 MB, highfi
# 108 MB, ...). Unfiltered that is a 1.2 GB upload for a build that needs ~25 MB.
#
# This list is deliberately explicit. The obvious version -- "/*" followed by
# "!/open-home/" -- is valid gitignore and git honours it, but it broke builds
# 27 and 28: EAS's walker prunes an excluded directory before it ever tests the
# re-include, so open-home/ never reached the archive. Do not reintroduce
# negation here; add new sibling projects to the list below instead.
#
# .easignore is only read at the archive root, i.e. this directory. A copy in
# apps/mobile/ is silently ignored.

# ---- the git history ----
# This is what kept the archive at 439 MB even after every sibling project was
# excluded. eas-cli does `git clone --depth 1` of the repo root, THEN deletes
# the worktree files that .easignore matches — but the clone's own .git still
# holds a pack of every tracked file in MonoClaw (~700 MB of travelog, projects,
# highfi). eas-cli removes that .git only when .easignore names it explicitly,
# which it deliberately does not do by default. The build does not need history.
#
# (node_modules needs no rule here: eas-cli always ignores it when copying the
# working directory. The earlier "node_modules/" lines below are harmless but
# were not what was inflating the upload.)
.git

# ---- sibling projects in this monorepo (not part of the iOS app) ----
/ActivityClaw/
/ContextClaw/
/MonoClaw/
/PayMe/
/activity-hub/
/activity-hub-test/
/admin-hub/
/agent-swarm-projects/
/agents/
/appcatalog/
/blog/
/cannon/
/ccut-gateway/
/chase/
/clawmap/
/config/
/core/
/croppa/
/dash-app/
/docker-agent-system/
/foreman/
/highfi/
/inkling/
/jobs/
/lumen/
/matts-claw-blog/
/media/
/meditation-app/
/memory/
/missions/
/monoclaw-dashboard/
/nightsweep/
/nyc-events/
/ora-health/
/ora-room-inspection/
/ora-swarm/
/portal/
/portfolio/
/portfolio-site/
/projects/
/raves/
/recilia-api/
/rolodex/
/rolodex-deploy/
/skill-builder/
/skills/
/test-files/
/tokens/
/travelog/
/twitter-plugin/
/vm-agent-system/
/waypoint/
/weather-app/

# ---- inside open-home ----
# EAS runs its own install from package-lock.json.
# Anchored forms alone did not work: build 29 still uploaded 439 MB, almost all
# of it node_modules. .easignore REPLACES .gitignore, so anything gitignored is
# otherwise pulled back in. The bare form matches at any depth and is the one
# EAS's walker honours.
node_modules/
/open-home/node_modules/
/open-home/**/node_modules/
# Enclosure CAD, renders and product mockups; never bundled in the app.
/open-home/hardware/
# The legacy web control surface and TV display: separate from the mobile app.
/open-home/apps/app/
/open-home/tv/
#
# services/cloud and services/hub stay: they are npm workspaces named in
# package-lock.json and `npm ci` fails on a lockfile mismatch without them.
# Together they are about 1 MB, so there is nothing to gain by cutting them.

# ---- never leaves this machine ----
/open-home/apps/mobile/creds/
/open-home/apps/mobile/credentials.json
**/*.p12
**/*.mobileprovision
**/.env
**/.env.*
